  "description_html": "Size comparison of various specimens of the large mosasaur <i>Tylosaurus</i>.  Total lenght and skull lenght based on<sup id=\"cite_ref-T.rex_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-T.rex-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> Silhouettes based on <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/randomdinos/art/Tylosaurus-rex-skeletal-reconstruction-1339180653\">Randomdinos T. rex</a>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Tylosaurus_rex\"><i>Tylosaurus rex</i></h4></div>\n<ul><li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#0066FF\" title=\"#0066FF\"> </b> <b>KUVP 5033</b> The \"Bunker\" specimen has been estimated to be 13.21 m in total length and has a total skull length of 1.63 m <sup id=\"cite_ref-T.rex_1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-T.rex-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Tylosaurus_(Hainosaurus?)_bernardi\"><span id=\"Tylosaurus_.28Hainosaurus.3F.29_bernardi\"></span><i>Tylosaurus (Hainosaurus?) bernardi</i></h4></div>\n<ul><li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#808080\" title=\"#808080\"> </b> <b>IRScNB R23</b> Holotype, estimated to be 11.64 m and has a total skull length of 1.38 m <sup id=\"cite_ref-T.rex_1-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-T.rex-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Tylosaurus_(Hainosaurus?)_saskatchweanensis\"><span id=\"Tylosaurus_.28Hainosaurus.3F.29_saskatchweanensis\"></span><i>Tylosaurus (Hainosaurus?) saskatchweanensis</i></h4></div>\n<ul><li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#C83737\" title=\"#C83737\"> </b> <b>RSM P2588.1</b> This specimen (nicknamed \"Omācīw\") has a skull length of 1.32 m (4.3 ft)<sup id=\"cite_ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> and a total length of around 9.75 m (32.0 ft).<sup id=\"cite_ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Tylosaurus_proriger\"><i>Tylosaurus proriger</i></h4></div>\n<ul><li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#003380\" title=\"#003380\"> </b> <b>KUVP 1032</b> Estimated to be 9.65 m and has a total skull length of 1.21 m <sup id=\"cite_ref-T.rex_1-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-T.rex-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Tylosaurus_(Hainosaurus?)_pembinensis\"><span id=\"Tylosaurus_.28Hainosaurus.3F.29_pembinensis\"></span><i>Tylosaurus (Hainosaurus?) pembinensis</i></h4></div>\n<ul><li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#37C871\" title=\"#37C871\"> </b> <b>MM V95</b> This specimen has a skull length of 1.21 m. Length estimates for this species are lacking, but the silhouette been based on the above skull length and revised vertebral count at 8.94 m.<sup id=\"cite_ref-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Tylosaurus_nepaeolicus\"><i>Tylosaurus nepaeolicus</i></h4></div>\n<ul><li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#FF7F2A\" title=\"#FF7F2A\"> </b> <b>AMNH FARB 2167</b>  Estimated to be 8.66 m and has a total skull length of 1.12 m. <sup id=\"cite_ref-T.rex_1-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-T.rex-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Tylosaurus_'borealis'\"><span id=\"Tylosaurus_.27borealis.27\"></span><i>Tylosaurus 'borealis'</i></h4></div>\n<p>This taxon was published in a thesis and is therefore currently invalid.\n</p>\n<ul><li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#7137C8\" title=\"#7137C8\"> </b> <b>TMP 2014.011.0001</b> Estimated to be 7.74 m and has a total skull length of 1 m. <sup id=\"cite_ref-T.rex_1-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-T.rex-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Tylosaurus_(Hainosaurus?)_gaudryi\"><span id=\"Tylosaurus_.28Hainosaurus.3F.29_gaudryi\"></span><i>Tylosaurus (Hainosaurus?) gaudryi</i></h4></div>\n<ul><li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#800000FF\" title=\"#800000FF\"> </b> <b>MNHN 1896–15)</b> Holotype, estimated to be 7.14 m and has a total skull length of 0.95 m <sup id=\"cite_ref-T.rex_1-6\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-T.rex-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Tylosaurus_kansasensis\"><i>Tylosaurus kansasensis</i></h4></div>\n<ul><li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#FFDD55\" title=\"#FFDD55\"> </b> <b>FHSM VP-13742</b> Largest specimen. Estimated to be 7 m and has a total skull length of 0.91 m. <sup id=\"cite_ref-T.rex_1-7\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-T.rex-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Tylosaurus_iembeensis\"><i>Tylosaurus iembeensis</i></h4></div>\n<ul><li><b style=\"display:inline-block;line-height:1.7;width:1.7em;margin-right:-1px;border:1px solid #808080;background:#FF00FFFF\" title=\"#FF00FFFF\"> </b> <b>MGUAN PA294</b> Largest specimen. Estimated to be 5.52 m and has a total skull length of 0.71 m. <sup id=\"cite_ref-T.rex_1-8\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-T.rex-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<p><br>\nThe diver silhoutte from <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scuba33.jpg\" title=\"File:Scuba33.jpg\">File:Scuba33.jpg</a>, which is by NOAA and in the public domain.\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"References\">References</h4></div>\n<ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-T.rex-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <a href=\"#cite_ref-T.rex_1-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-T.rex_1-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-T.rex_1-2\"><sup><i><b>c</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-T.rex_1-3\"><sup><i><b>d</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-T.rex_1-4\"><sup><i><b>e</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-T.rex_1-5\"><sup><i><b>f</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-T.rex_1-6\"><sup><i><b>g</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-T.rex_1-7\"><sup><i><b>h</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-T.rex_1-8\"><sup><i><b>i</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\"> (2026). \"A gigantic new species of <i>Tylosaurus</i> (Squamata, Mosasauridae) from Texas : and a revised character list for phylogenetic analyses of Mosasauridae\". <i>Bulletin of the American Museum of Natural History</i> (482): 1–77. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISSN\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:ISSN\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">ISSN</span></a></span> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.worldcat.org/issn/0003-0090\">0003-0090</a>.</cite></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">Jiménez-Huidobro, Paulina; Caldwell, Michael W.; Paparella, Ilaria; Bullard, Timon S. (2019). \"A new species of tylosaurine mosasaur from the upper Campanian Bearpaw Formation of Saskatchewan, Canada\". <i>Journal of Systematic Palaeontology</i> <b>17</b> (10): 849-864.</cite></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-3\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20201001163347/https://royalsaskmuseum.ca/rsm/visit/exhibits/travelling-exhibits/omcw\">Omācīw</a>. <i>Royal Saskatchewan Museum</i>. Royal Saskatchewan Museum (2020). Archived from <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://royalsaskmuseum.ca/rsm/visit/exhibits/travelling-exhibits/omcw\">the original</a> on <span class=\"mw-formatted-date\" title=\"2020-10-01\">2020-10-01</span>. Retrieved on <span class=\"mw-formatted-date\" title=\"2020-07-29\">2020-07-29</span>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-4\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-4\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">Bullard, Timon S.; Caldwell, Michael W. (2010). \"Redescription and rediagnosis of the tylosaurine mosasaur <i>Hainosaurus pembinensis</i> Nicholls, 1988, as <i>Tylosaurus pembinensis</i> (Nicholls, 1988)\". <i>Journal of Vertebrate Paleontology</i> <b>30</b> (2): 416-426.</cite></span>\n</li>\n</ol>",
